Trace the following program to see what it writes:
const text = 'id=800';
console.log(/\d+/.test(text));
What boolean is printed?

The team wants to know what this code logs:
const arr = [801, 2, 3];
console.log(arr.includes(801));
What does the log show?

The library helper below is called once:
const arr = [802, 7, 2];
arr.push(67);
console.log(arr.length);
On this input, what number is printed by the final log?

Try to predict the result of running this code:
const arr = [803, 14, 90, 50];
const part = arr.slice(1, 3);
console.log(part.length);
From this trace, explain what this code prints and why that value follows from the language rules.

Evaluate from top to bottom:
const arr = [804, 14, 47, 94, 26];
const removed = arr.splice(1, 2);
console.log(arr.length);
What length is logged after splice mutates arr?

A diagnostic run executes the code as written:
const arr = [805, 7];
const out = arr.map(x => x * 2);
console.log(out[0]);
